Given circuit is, <img src="img/abc18092160f75e1.webp" loading="lazy" alt="" style="width:min(100%,256px)"> Given input voltage, \(v_{i}(t)=10\sin 314t\) Hence the peak value is \(V_{m}=10\,\text{V}\) During the positive half cycle, the diode conducts and charges the capacitor to the peak value of the input voltage. Therefore, \(V_{C}=10\,\text{V}\) and the voltage across voltmeter is zero. During the negative half cycle, the diode becomes reverse biased and the capacitor retains its charge because the voltmeter draws negligible current. Hence the voltage across voltmeter is \[V_i(t) - V_C = (10\sin 314t - 10)\, \text{ V}\] Therefore the voltage across the voltmeter (diode) is a half-wave waveform whose voltage varies from \(0\,\text{ V}\) to \(-20\,\text{V}\) An ideal moving iron voltmeter reads the RMS value of the applied voltage. RMS value of this waveform is \[V_{\text{RMS}}=\sqrt{\frac{1}{2\pi}
\int_{\pi}^{2\pi}(10\sin \theta-10)^2\,d\theta}\, \hspace{1cm}\text{ where } \theta = 314t\] \[=
\sqrt{
\frac{100}{2\pi}
\int_{\pi}^{2\pi}
(\sin\theta-1)^2\,d\theta
}\] \[=
\sqrt{
\frac{100}{2\pi}
\int_{\pi}^{2\pi}
\left(
\sin^2\theta-2\sin\theta+1
\right)d\theta
}\] Using, \[\int_{\pi}^{2\pi}\sin^2\theta\,d\theta=\frac{\pi}{2}, 
\int_{\pi}^{2\pi}\sin\theta\,d\theta=-2,
\int_{\pi}^{2\pi}1\,d\theta=\pi\] Therefore, \[V_{\text{RMS}}
=
\sqrt{
\frac{100}{2\pi}
\left(
\frac{\pi}{2}+4+\pi
\right)
}\] \[=
\sqrt{
\frac{100}{2\pi}
\left(
\frac{3\pi}{2}+4
\right)
}\] \[=
10
\sqrt{
\frac{1}{2\pi}
\left(
\frac{3\pi}{2}+4
\right)
}\] \[V_{\text{RMS}}
\approx
12.24\,\text{V}\] \[\boxed{\text{(B)}\quad 12.24\,\text{V}}\] <div class="sol-block sol-keypoints"><div class="sol-block-title">Key points</div><ul><li>Moving iron instruments respond to RMS value.</li></ul></div>

The given circuit is a common-collector (emitter follower) amplifier. The mid-band voltage gain of an emitter follower is \[A_v=\frac{V_o}{V_i}
=\frac{I_B(1+h_{fe})R_E}
{I_B\left[h_{ie}+(1+h_{fe})R_E\right]}\] Since \((1+h_{fe})R_E\gg h_{ie},\) \[A_v
=\frac{(1+h_{fe})R_E}
{h_{ie}+(1+h_{fe})R_E}
\approx1\] \[\boxed{(C)\;\approx1}\] <img src="img/d88ada27e24e34a5.webp" loading="lazy" alt="" style="width:min(100%,608px)">
